{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779133948,"nonce":"XAyLLLAYY7Ysm+O62KtWTOwYaoE=","title":"Studio Scenario Workspace Slice 1: entity registry, selection bus, and inspector","message":"## Parent\n\nChild of `5378a5d`, comment `503c7f8`.\n\n## Purpose\n\nCreate the shared scenario-authoring foundation for the Scenario Projection Workspace. The goal is to stop treating graph-node selection as the only top-pane selection model and introduce canonical scenario entities that future Graph, Workspace, and Objectives projections can share.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Introduce or formalize a normalized scenario entity registry over existing graph/task/objective/probe state.\n- Add a top-pane selection model for selected entity ID, hovered entity ID, active projection, active stage/scenario, and future pinned inspector state.\n- Map graph nodes, graph ports or wires where practical, taps/probes, task placeholders, mechanics placeholders, and objective terms into canonical entity IDs.\n- Convert the right inspector to render from selected scenario entity kind rather than directly from graph-only assumptions.\n- Keep bottom-pane run/evaluation selection separate from top-pane scenario selection.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Selecting a graph node/tap/edge updates the canonical top-pane selection.\n- The inspector can render graph nodes, taps/probes, edges, task placeholders, mechanics placeholders, and objective terms through one scenario entity path.\n- The selection model can represent entity kinds needed by later Workspace and Objectives projections even when some projections are not implemented yet.\n- Existing graph editing still works.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Add unit tests for entity registry and selection helpers.\n- Run focused frontend tests.\n- Run `npm run build` from `web`.\n\n## Branch\n\nSuggested feature branch: `feature/studio-scenario-slice1-entities`.","files":null}]}